ed to continue to social distance  and put health and welfare  first and foremost but not at the  expense of expressing  uh their right to vote and the point of  view on who should lead our country  now let's talk about sofi and personal  finance your campaign is to get your  money  right and as we know in my generation  a lot of us get it wrong and it's not  only our fault all the time  i know i just finished business school  and i put myself in an extra 150  000 worth of debt for it so when you  look at your client base  what is the thing they're struggling  with the most yeah so we're we're  targeting millennials and gen z's high  achievers people  that do have second degrees that can't  get to the point where they have enough  money to do what they want whether  that's having children or buy a house or  or change careers because they've  burdened themselves with a lot of debt  or they haven't invested or they haven't  budget appropriately  and so we're really servicing  individuals needs across  borrowing saving spending investing and  protecting  and helping them make better choices  along that spectrum  so before you even take out a college  loan how much  can you afford to take out from a  student loan perspective  based on the career you'll have when  you're done with school and so that's  why we launched in school loans  student loan financing is for those like  yourself that have really taken on a  significant economic burden  and how do we lower the cost of that  burden so that you can start investing  it's really critical to have  accessibility to investing in your 20s  and to start investing  and having the income to do that because  it will compound over the next several  decades and put you in a much better  position as you enter your 30s and 40s  put you in a better position to be able  to buy a house to have children and  potentially uh retire early  so we're really helping people across  the entire spectrum which is why  on our mobile phone we have