ng  i think people still have challenges  clearly over the last nine months  everyone's sort of changed their routine  changed their way of living and adapted  for the first time in many of their  lives they were left with no income  whatsoever  at no fault of their own and it happened  overnight so  we have seen a huge acceleration in the  need for digital uh financial services  that sofi provides offering your mobile  phone  we've had five quarters of accelerating  year-over-year growth in our member base  uh we're up to seventy percent  year-over-year growth and we've seen an  increase  every quarter um since over the last  five quarters  part of that is we're offering all these  new products but part of that is people  also needing for the first time  all of their financial services at their  fingertips on their mobile phone  um and what so far we provide not just  the products but also the ability to  talk to a certified financial planner  and schedule that from your phone the  ability to talk to a career  consultant from corn ferry through a  partnership the ability to attend  zoom events on thinking about retirement  thinking about budgeting during this  time period so  the need is still great and will  continue to be greater than it's been  um for financial services for people to  get their money right  so one of those ways that people have  been using their money  in a big way during this pandemic is  we've seen a lot of people  enter the stock market we've seen retail  trading  like we haven't seen in many many years  how is that  impacting you we've definitely seen an  acceleration in people  opening up a sofi invest account and  buying stocks and setting up recurring  investments and  and investing in diversified portfolios  like the sofi giga economy etf and  uh select 500 etf and others and that's  really important i think it reflects a  couple of things first interest rates  are basically zero  so getting an inch you know return on  your savings or ch