 also benefiting as people  are staying at home they're thinking  about changing their home  and restructuring in a way that's got  greater utility and greater value  and so we do see people taking out  unsecured personal loans  to finance a home remodeling but in low  and straight environments it's really  student loans that are being refinanced  mortgages that are being refinanced and  people investing  now what has all of this taught you  what is all of these new products that  you're adding on to sofi  teaching you about how to build the bank  of the future  is there anything about the current  financial industry that's just not  working that needs to be re-envisioned  from your perspective  yeah the reason why we call our  customers members is that it's about  building a lifelong relationship with  them it's about  understanding their needs and the market  that we think that's open that no one  has filled is this a relationship  approach  to personal financial services it's a  shame that you can do incredibly well  academically do well professionally and  not have enough money  to have children or to buy a house or  retire early and so we're focused on  helping those people that have done all  the things they're supposed to  better manage their money so they can  get it get it right and therefore  accomplish  their ambitions and so the one thing  that's very clear  is that having a relationship is paying  dividends more than 60  of the mortgages that we are processing  and funding  are from our existing members um we're  also seeing a huge uptick  in the number of people that have  multiple products with sofi we're seeing  about 350 percent year-over-year growth  in what we call multi-product members  and so we had a thesis going into this  that there's a part of the world that's  underserved  that part of the world needs to have a  relationship approach to it  we've brought our full suite of product  approach to the table for them because  we need to be there 