ar  do you have more mergers in your future  um  we're really focused on you know  integrating both of those uh  acquisitions that are going quite well  and and marching across our five  priorities and so  uh nothing on the horizon right now but  we're really happy with  the progress we've made on both fronts  and see a significant opportunity  for us broadly the galileo acquisition  really has two parts it allows us to  innovate faster in the front end with  sofi money  but it also allows us to provide  stability for the overall  industry of digital first uh banking or  digital first cma accounts  um and it's giving us an opportunity to  expand into international markets  uh we're open in latin with three big  partners we're excited about that we'll  be looking at  other latin countries in addition to  mexico where we are today and we've just  seen an acceleration the demand for  galileo's payment platform  uh to enable people to provide financial  services like a checking or savings  account or cma account and we're seeing  the demand from a variety of different  channels not just  new uh companies but existing companies  outside of finance  and also big big banks and so the  opportunities  is as vast and as strong as we thought  it was in fact  exceeding our expectations and  digital i mean that's the big word  during this pandemic banking digitally  we still see some of these huge banks  with major branch networks  even at so far you have a lot of uh  connectivity you still have people that  are  able to talk to your clients here as  they figure out their future  how fast does this digital conversion go  i mean  how what what's the next stage of  fintech  sure um so the interesting thing about  the evolution of financial services from  physical  digital is that unlike the other  categories like  e-commerce and online travel and digital  media and social  there still hasn't been a company that  we would define as winner take most  and we think our approach to the